stmuseer.dk/","wp":"da:Skagens Museum","ds":"Skagens Museum is an art museum in Skagen, Denmark, that exhibits an extensive collection of works by members of the colony of Skagen Painters who lived and worked in the area in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Important artists include Marie and P. S. Krøyer, Anna and Michael Ancher, Laurits Tuxen, Viggo Johansen, and Holger Drachmann. The museum also hosts special exhibitions.","wpu":"Skagens Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Skagens_Museum%2C_entrance%2C_2015-07-28.jpg/960px-Skagens_Museum%2C_entrance%2C_2015-07-28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Skagen Vandtårn","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.725506,"lo":10.596872,"d":646,"h":"week 22-35 11:00-17:00","wp":"da:Vandtårnet i Skagen"},{"n":"Anchers Hus","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.726115,"lo":10.596908,"d":701,"wp":"da:Anchers Hus","ds":"Anchers Hus is an art museum and gallery situated in the former residence of the painters Michael and Anna Ancher in Skagen, Denmark. Anchers Hus is located on Markvej in Skagen, Denmark.","wpu":"Anchers Hus","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Michael_%26_Anna_Anchers_Hus_i_Skagen%2C_2007_ubt.jpeg/960px-Michael_%26_Anna_Anchers_Hus_i_Skagen%2C_2007_ubt.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Skagen Bamsemuseum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.725756,"lo":10.597853,"d":705,"wp":"da:Skagen Bamsemuseum"},{"n":"Villa Pax","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.718778,"lo":10.577843,"d":763,"wp":"da:Drachmanns Hus"},{"n":"Kystmuseet Skagen","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.71642,"lo":10.574527,"d":1050,"h":"Tu-Fr 10:00-16:00; PH,Sa 11:00-16:00; Su,Mo off","w":"https://www.kystmuseet.dk/besoeg-os/kystmuseet-skagen"},{"n":"Kragskov Mølle","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.716265,"lo":10.574084,"d":1081},{"n":"Skagens Vippefyr","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.726796,"lo":10.608212,"d":1258,"wp":"en:Skagen's Vippefyr","ds":"Skagen's Vippefyr (sometimes referred to in English as Skagen's Lever Light) is a navigational light mechanism located in Skagen in the far north of Jutland. The original vippefyr, the first of its kind, was built in 1627. A faithful copy now stands on the same site.","wpu":"Skagen's Vippefyr","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Bascule-ight-Skagen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Skagen Odde Naturcenter","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.740013,"lo":10.595518,"d":2139,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-16:00; Sa,Su 11:00-16:00","w":"https://www.skagen-natur.dk/","wp":"da:Skagen Odde Naturcenter"},{"n":"Den Tilsandede Kirke","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.713622,"lo":10.550564,"d":2481,"wp":"da:Den tilsandede kirke"},{"n":"Flagbakken","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.718817,"lo":10.545331,"d":2663},{"n":"Stokmile","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.705694,"lo":10.552824,"d":2787},{"n":"Skagen Fyr","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.735496,"lo":10.630185,"d":2879,"wp":"da:Skagen Fyr"},{"n":"Skagen Fuglestation","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.735526,"lo":10.630495,"d":2896,"w":"https://www.skagenfuglestation.dk/"},{"n":"Det Grå Fyr","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.735602,"lo":10.630435,"d":2898,"h":"Mo-Su 10:00-17:00","w":"https://www.detgraafyr.dk/"},{"n":"Skagen Naturhistoriske Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.719892,"lo":10.537829,"d":3100,"wp":"da:Skagen Naturhistoriske Museum"},{"n":"Skagen Bunkermuseum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.738913,"lo":10.631823,"d":3183,"w":"https://skagen-bunkermuseum.dk/","wp":"da:Skagen Bunkermuseum"},{"n":"Grenen Kunstmuseum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.739739,"lo":10.634037,"d":3343,"w":"https://galleri-grenen.dk/","ph":"+45 29784981","wp":"da:Grenen Kunstmuseum"},{"n":"Drachmanns Grav","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.73943,"lo":10.636361,"d":3431},{"n":"Skagen Fugle